diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ac40a2ecba9abb83e51b9a6e407d5b5155271084..f775a4556b5e202cd32cac46a5a857588ce53249 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -21,4 +21,17 @@ returns `{ items: ["first", "second"] }`. Invalid patches, unresolved paths, and
 failed tests throw errors. An empty path targets the whole document; removing
 the root returns `undefined`, and a subsequent root `add` can restore it.
 
+Operations are evaluated in order and stop at the first error; a failed patch
+leaves both inputs unchanged. `move` resolves its destination after removing its
+source, and cannot move a value into one of its descendants. `test` compares JSON
+values structurally, ignoring object member order. Members not defined for an
+operation are ignored.
+
+Pass JSON values directly: finite numbers, strings, booleans, null, dense arrays,
+and plain objects (including objects with a null prototype). Operation objects
+must also be plain objects, with their required members as own properties.
+Sparse arrays, cycles, and non-JSON values such as `undefined` are errors in the
+document or required `value` members. Arrays are read by their own indexed
+elements, regardless of custom iterators or inherited elements.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or later, with native TypeScript support).
